# NEL Vocabulary — enforced

The source content describes the lab through three overlapping taxonomies and
uses *programme*, *package*, *profile*, *panel* and *checkup* interchangeably.
That ambiguity does not enter this codebase.

A bare ambiguous noun in a table name, type name, route path or field name is a
**defect**, not a style preference.

## Forbidden bare nouns

```
test · result · patient · branch · unit · programme · package · profile
panel · checkup · device · offer · service · user · admin · content · item
```

## Qualified replacements

| Forbidden | Use |
|---|---|
| `test` | `LabTest` for the domain entity. `spec` for a software test file. |
| `result` | **Forbidden as a domain noun.** `ResultsPortalLink` is the only permitted compound. Anything else is a boundary defect. |
| `patient` | **Forbidden.** Site users are `Visitor`. Dashboard users are `Operator`. |
| `branch` | `Branch` as an exact PascalCase entity only. Lowercase means git. |
| `unit` | `LabUnit` |
| `programme` / `package` / `profile` / `panel` / `checkup` | `Programme` is canonical. The rest are source-content synonyms, never identifiers. |
| `tier` | `ProgrammeTier` — Silver · Gold · Platinum · Children |
| `device` | `Equipment` — `device` collides with viewport and user-device |
| `offer` | `Offer`, PascalCase entity only |
| `service` | Forbidden outright. The 2018 site used it three inconsistent ways. |
| `content` | Name the entity. |

`Branch` · `Offer` · `Equipment` · `Programme` · `LabTest` · `LabUnit` ·
`Visitor` · `Operator` are permitted as exact PascalCase entity names only.
Lowercase use as a bare field or noun is a defect.

**Why `patient` and `result` are banned outright:** the cheapest place to catch a
boundary violation is at the identifier. If a `results` table is ever written,
this rule catches it before the security review does.
